WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.200
Hey, so this, this is really concerning and
it goes to the heart of what I've been talking

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:13.980
about for a while, the last few years about
purity tests and self destructive behavior.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.040
By the left.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.380
Um, I did a video a few weeks ago where I
said I'm for Medicare for all.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.080
I've been for it for a decade.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:29.250
I think it's one of, if not the best option,
it's a crisis that we have medical bankruptcy

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.250
in this country.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:35.579
I mean, I want to see this happen, but it's
going to be way harder than simply Bernie

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:39.850
becomes president and we get Medicare for
all and we need to know that and we need to

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.760
be up for that fight.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.219
And there were a bunch of people who wrote
to me who said, David being a defeatist, you're

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:47.850
a centrist shill.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:51.620
You're providing cover for not advocating
for Medicare for all.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.340
And of course, none of those things are true.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.370
And I wasn't doing any of those things.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:01.969
Now, people who have been watching this show
for awhile know that not only am I for Medicare

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:08.400
for all, I've been advocating for it publicly
on this program as Medicare for all since

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.170
at least 2015 but remember that Medicare for
all is a term that became more popular in

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.740
the last four years.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.820
Even before that we were really talking about
the same thing when we were calling it single

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.820
payer.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:25.630
And in that sense I have been advocating for
this since 2011 publicly if not longer.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:31.340
Uh, then over the weekend in a compilation
video of some kind, I don't know the orange

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:36.189
origins of this video or the oranges of it,
to quote Donald Trump, it has about 50,000

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:37.189
views.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:43.729
As of this recording, my video comes up in
a compilation of people who do not support

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:48.759
Medicare for all, including Joe Biden and
peed Buddha judge, and at least as framed

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:55.729
by this video, Elizabeth Warren, I am included
as an opponent of Medicare for all.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:59.909
Here's a few seconds of this video, which
includes audio of my clips, sort of mixed

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:02.970
in with other people who are not for Medicare
for all.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.750
Take a look, a voter's choice to opt in to
care for.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:11.260
I am here to talk to [inaudible] guys.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.420
If I'm the enemy, we're not going to win.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:20.129
If I, as someone who has been calling for
single payer and Medicare for all for nearly

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:23.580
a decade publicly, the videos are up.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:30.460
If I am the enemy because I refuse to Gaslight
my audience and I choose to be real about

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.170
what it will take to get Medicare for all.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:38.300
If I am considered the opposition to Medicare
for all, we will lose.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:44.490
We have lost, we've gotten so far down this
with us or against us.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:51.599
Everything is black, white rabbit hole that
uh, uh, I am being included in a compilation

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.080
of opponents of Medicare for all.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.810
And this is how allies get pushed out.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.810
Okay?

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:03.130
If I'm on the wrong side of this, then consider
who is on the right side.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.140
I mean, almost no one, right?

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:08.270
If you're against Medicare for all, you're
of course on the wrong side.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.780
And I agree with that.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:15.980
If you think Medicare for all simply can't
work economically, you're on the wrong side.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.310
There may be some tweaks that have to be made
to the proposals and I've pointed them out,

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.989
but if you just simply think it doesn't work,
you're on the wrong side.

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:23.629
It works in many countries.

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:28.150
If you're okay with Medicare for all, but
also okay with other other systems according

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.230
to this black white litmus test, you're on
the wrong side.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.819
If you're for Medicare for all but like me
believe it is going to be way more difficult

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:38.500
than some on the left are willing to admit.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.730
Apparently you're also on the wrong side.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:46.099
If you have like me been advocating for Medicare
for all publicly for a decade, but you believe

00:03:46.099 --> 00:03:49.860
there are too many people who misunderstand
what it will take to get there.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.830
I guess I'm also on the wrong side, so who
are you left with?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.600
This is how you get a purity test.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.569
We're the only people on, I guess the right
side are those who are not only for Medicare

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:08.319
for all at the exclusion of any other idea,
a priori, but who also shut their mouths and

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:12.760
don't get real about what it's going to take
to get there, including recognizing that Bernie

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.150
becoming president alone isn't going to do
it.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:20.371
I guess my choices now are because I've been,
by virtue of doing a realistic assessment

00:04:20.371 --> 00:04:25.960
of what it will take, pushed into the anti
Medicare for all camp, I can either comply

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.220
with the purity test or shut my mouth, right?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:33.950
I mean, what I need to start broadcasting
Medicare for all is the way, and if we elect

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.240
Bernie, we will have it in four years.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:41.250
Even if I believe that to be absolutely untrue,
especially if the first two of those years

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.560
we don't even have control of the Senate.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.910
Is that what I'm supposed to do?

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:50.380
Tell what I believe to be lies to my audience.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.140
That's not what I do, right?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.070
I call things as they see them.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.310
I'm a supporter of Medicare for all.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.520
I've been one for a decade.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:05.360
But if this analysis is what gets me branded
as an enemy of Medicare for all, what are

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.190
we even doing to our movement?

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.140
What are we doing to ourselves?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:13.770
If I'm the enemy on Medicare for all, Trump
is going to get himself reelected and sweep.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:17.390
I mean this, it's just such a misguided, uh,
effort.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:25.670
Republicans, you know, Trump does insane,
dangerous stuff and Trumpists laugh and they

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:26.670
don't care.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.900
And they say, Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:34.620
But then I can't even talk about the difficulty
of Medicare for all without getting smeared

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:39.240
as being against it or hurting the movement
because I'm being realistic.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.710
Say hello to another four years of Trump.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.300
If this is what our movement is doing, it's,
it's heartbreaking.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.820
It's so sad.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.560
Um, but I don't even know where to go.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:56.040
[inaudible] it's the, the idea of me being,
you know, the enemy on this issue tells us

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.800
that at least for a sliver of the left, and
I don't believe I got a lot of positive emails

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.050
and, and appreciation for my commentary, but
at least to a sliver of the left,

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:11.280
uh, merely realistic assessments are now considered
being on the other side.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.410
We're in trouble, folks.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.100
We're in real trouble.

